<tbody>
<tr> 
<td width="100%" valign="top" align="center" style="padding: 0px; width: 100%;"> <p height="20" width="100%" style="mso-line-height-rule:exactly; mso-table-lspace:0pt; mso-table-rspace:0pt; text-size-adjust:100%; width: 100%; height: 20px; max-height: 20px; margin: 0px; font-size: 20px; line-height: 20px"> &nbsp; </p> </td> 
</tr> 
<tr> 
<td width="100%" valign="top" align="left" style="text-align: left; font-family: Chivo, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #223341; font-size: 24px; font-weight: bold; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 26px; padding-bottom: 20px; width: 100%;"> <p style="margin: 0px; text-align: center;"><span style="color: #48b985; font-size: 24px; line-height: 26px;">Advice To Finance Leaders On A Clear Path To Exit From Flywire's CFO Mike Ellis</span></p> </td> 
</tr> 
<tr> 
<td width="100%" valign="top" align="left" class="aligned-bullets" style="text-align: left; font-family: Chivo, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; color: #223341; font-size: 16px; font-weight: normal; letter-spacing: normal; line-height: 24px; padding-bottom: 40px; width: 100%;"> <p style="margin: 0px;">‌<br /></p> <p style="margin: 0px;">Hello&nbsp;{{lead.First Name:default= }},</p> <p style="margin: 0px;">‌<br /></p> <p style="margin: 0px;">A few weeks ago, our CFO Mike Ellis had the opportunity to share his journey on taking Flywire public at Ascent’s Spotlight on Finance virtual conference. The discussion revolved around the planning needed to prepare your company for an eventual IPO, merger, or acquisition.</p> <p style="margin: 0px;">‌<br /></p> <p style="margin: 0px;"><strong>If your company is planning to go public, Ellis recommends:</strong></p> <p style="margin: 0px;">‌<br /></p> 
<ol style="margin-left: 15px; padding-left: 0px; list-style-position: inside; margin-bottom: 0px !important; margin-top: 0px !important;"> 
<li>Talk to the CFOs, VP of Finance, and other senior leaders in your finance network for mentorship and guidance (Ellis met with a CFO weekly while taking Flywire public)</li> 
<li>Strengthening your teams’ fiber is crucial, so focus on hiring strong talent</li> 
<li>Set up internal processes and controls, regardless of how early you are in the process, that can give you the appropriate internal control structure and ability to forecast</li> 
</ol> <p style="margin: 0px;">‌<br /></p> <p style="margin: 0px;">Want to catch a recap of the Spotlight on Finance talk?</p> </td> 
</tr> 
<tr> 
<td width="100%" valign="top" align="center" class="minw-158 hover-green" style="width: 100%;"> 
